// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2325208268" "I give up. Ok? Just... Just don't hit me."
// Answer Text :
"P155240288" "Ask about the clockwork."
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"
// Page ClockworkPage1 Text :
"P4265327182" "The clockwork... Yeah, they came through here, along with the Clockwork King. He busted us up real bad, I can still hear his voice ringing in my head."
// Answer Text :
"P2953807680" "Ask what the Clockwork King said."
// Page ClockworkPage2 Text :
"P30130377" "He was screaming about us trying to poison his princess, or something. I didn't really get a chance to ask him to repeat himself before he blasted me with some sort of psychic bolt, then everything went black."
// Answer Text :
"P2184296939" "Ask about the poison."
// Page PoisonPage1 Text :
"P4245051952" "Doctor Vahzilok has us all over Faultline moving these canisters of his new cocktail toward the dam. We were planning on dumping it into the water supply."
// Answer Text :
"P2451685708" "Ask what the poison does."
// Page PoisonPage2 Text :
"P2441560081" "Well, according to Vahzilok it will make the people of Paragon City 'more accepting of his blessing', but you know what? I don't care anymore. That guy is a lunatic.<br><br>Blessing? Ha! They're just lab mice for his own twisted god complex."
// Answer Text :
"P791056046" "Ask about the change in loyalty."
// Page LoyaltyPage1 Text :
"P1834115952" "You know, I'm not sure, but I think the Clockwork King fighting to save his 'princess' made me think things through. I mean, these are people we're talking about. The Clockwork King gets it, I guess, sorta, I don't know why I didn't realize that what I was doing was so wrong until now.<br><br>Besides... there's no way I'm stopping you from taking me to the Zig, and that's the only place I'll be safe from Doctor Vahzilok when he finds out I revealed his plans to you."
// Answer Text :
"P2043071004" "Arrest him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2334325475" "Time is of the essence, {TaskForceName}. The Circle of Thorns have retreated back to Oranbega, so we'll have to wait for them to make the next move. The Clockwork, however, are still a very real threat. We'll need to weaken their presence in Faultline if we are going to prevent them from continuing their efforts to destroy the Faultline Dam.<br><br>The Circle may have knocked us down a peg, but we aren't out of the fight, not by a long shot."
// AcceptString :
"P1176714488" "Let's stop the clockwork!"
// SendOffString :
"P3364503675" "That's the spirit, {TaskForceName}. <br><br>I have <color yellow>Mirror Spirit</color> working in Faultline to look into any activities by the Circle of Thorns. Right now we'll focus on tracking down the Clockwork and the Vahzilok.<br><br><color LightGreen>Valkryie says that heroes have been reporting a large amount of clockwork going into one of the sewers here in Steel Canyon led by an Assembler Prince called Constructor. I have a feeling they're up to something regarding their Faultline project. </color><br><br>While you check it out, Valkryie and I will keep an eye out for any Vahzilok activities in the other parts of Steel Canyon. They'll be trying to move their operations shortly into Faultline, I'm sure."
// TaskTitle :
"P172360407" "<color deepskyblue>Dam Heroes</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3129909647" "<color deepskyblue>Part One: Rumble in the Sewers</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1765016853" "Stop Clockwork in the Sewers"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1438703597" "I'd love to help, {TaskForceName}, but someone needs to make sure the Vahzilok don't make any sudden moves."

